# Copy to .env (gitignored). Everything has a working default.
#
# THIS FILE IS READ ON RANK 0 ONLY. Both ranks are launched from up.sh on this
# node, so there is no second .env to keep in step - that is the point.
#
# NOTE the ordering trap, which bit the upstream project: up.sh does
# `set -a; . ./.env; set +a`, so .env OVERRIDES the environment. `FOO=x ./up.sh`
# is silently ignored for any key .env already defines. Edit the file, or check
# the summary lines up.sh prints before it launches.

# HF_TOKEN=hf_...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PATCH SITUATION, because it decides what actually runs
#
# Two patches are mandatory and are NOT written - they rewrite source inside
# the image. up.sh refuses to launch without them. See patches/README.md and
# ./extract-sources.sh. This is the first thing to deal with.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CHECKPOINT. Three publishers ship these weights, and they differ in
# SERIALISATION rather than in the weights - which is exactly why there are
# five patches. Pick with the patch cost in mind:
#
#   nvidia/...          133 GB / 11 shards.  BF16 dense + NVFP4 experts + FP8
#                       PLE. The default. Needs the MTP layer alias AND the
#                       FP8_BLOCK_SCALES MoE branch for speculative decoding -
#                       the preflight refuses in milliseconds if the latter is
#                       missing, so run it with MTP off until it is written.
#   RadixArk/...        126 GB / 206 shards. BF16 attention + FP8 PLE. Their
#                       README's KV-cache measurements are on this one.
#   local-inference-lab 99 GB / 37 shards.   MXFP8 attention + NVFP4 PLE. The
#                       old name of those weights; no longer resolves offline.
# MODEL=nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4
# SERVED_NAME=qwen3.8-flash-next

# Only if detection gets it wrong. up.sh recovers this from the checkpoint with
# ./detect-ple-dtype.py and re-injects it under text_config via --hf-overrides,
# because nvidia/... declares its FP8 PLE only inside config_groups. Setting it
# by hand overrides that.
# PLE_EMBEDDING_DTYPE=fp8

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE TWO NUMBERS THAT TRADE, and on this model they trade differently from
# every other workspace here.
#
# WEIGHTS ARE THE BINDING CONSTRAINT, NOT KV. ~64.5 GiB of weights per GPU
# against ~101.6 GiB budgeted leaves ~32 GiB of KV - which holds 2.13M bf16
# tokens, i.e. a 262K context over eight times. Of 48 layers only every 4th is
# full attention; the other 36 are Gated-DeltaNet, whose state is per REQUEST
# and not per token. So raising MAX_NUM_SEQS is cheap here and raising
# MAX_MODEL_LEN is what actually costs.
# MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144
# MAX_NUM_SEQS=8
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.835
#
# 0.835 is the reference kit's measured value. The GLM-5.3 workspace had to
# come DOWN from its recipe's number because a node running a desktop session
# missed the free-memory check by under a GiB, and rank 0 then reported the
# peer's death as a gloo "Connection closed by peer" - which points at the
# network rather than at the memory. If rank 1 dies about a minute in, this is
# the first knob.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KV DTYPE. `auto` (bf16) is the default HERE and fp8 is the reference default.
#
# fp8 is worth 1.70x the tokens per GiB - 3,652,200 against 2,131,159 measured
# on the reference kit - and it does NOT work on this image unmodified: the
# stock QSA kernels declare supported_kv_cache_dtypes = ["auto", "bfloat16"]
# and raise rather than degrade. The patch that lifts that is AGPL and was not
# ported (docs/decisions.md#qwen38-flash-next).
#
# When it exists, it is a QUALITY trade and not only a capacity one - quantised
# keys change which blocks the sparse indexer selects. Measure, do not assume:
#   ws up quant-quality-ab
# KV_CACHE_DTYPE=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MTP SPECULATIVE DECODING. 2.13x on batch-1 decode on the reference kit, at
# 72.8% acceptance decaying 89% / 74.5% / 60% by draft position.
#
# THAT DECAY IS THE HEALTH CHECK. A wrong expert block shape shows up as
# near-random acceptance rather than as a crash, and a broken draft path costs
# speed and nothing else - the target model verifies every token, so output
# stays perfectly correct at half the speed. Read it per position:
#   BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8896/v1 ws up spec-decode-accept
#
# 0 disables. Required today on nvidia/... until the FP8_BLOCK_SCALES MoE
# branch is written - the preflight will tell you.
# MTP_NUM_SPECULATIVE_TOKENS=3
#
# Their multi-token note, worth knowing: MTP > 1 logs "running multiple times
# of forward on same MTP layer, which may result in lower acceptance rate", and
# the QSA backend cannot fuse multi-step draft decode - it rebuilds attention
# metadata per draft step. 1 is the safe comparison point.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE 1M-CONTEXT PATH, and what it costs
#
# 262144 is native. YaRN extends it, and their own README calls the shipped
# 1M/8-seq combination oversubscribed: 8M cache tokens asked for against a
# 3.65M pool. vLLM preempts and re-prefills rather than failing, so the symptom
# is "the model got slow", not an error.
#
# Their four honest operating points:
#   deep, sequential   MAX_MODEL_LEN=1000000  MAX_NUM_SEQS=2
#   1M + concurrency   MAX_MODEL_LEN=1000000  MAX_NUM_SEQS=3  + --kv-cache-memory
#   throughput/agentic MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144   MAX_NUM_SEQS=8   <- the default here
#   middle ground      MAX_MODEL_LEN=512000   MAX_NUM_SEQS=4
#
# AND TREAT 1M AS UNVALIDATED. Their YaRN override sat at the top level of
# --hf-overrides for months, where vLLM setattr'd it onto the parent config and
# it never reached text_config - so every earlier "1M context" run was serving
# 1M positions on UNSCALED rope. up.sh nests it correctly, which means 1M here
# has genuinely never been measured by anyone.
# MAX_MODEL_LEN=1000000
# YARN_ENABLE=true
# YARN_FACTOR=4.0
#
# YaRN at or below native context costs accuracy and buys nothing. up.sh
# ignores YARN_ENABLE there and says so rather than passing it through.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Preflight. Aborts if another process holds a GPU on EITHER node - which
# `ws check` cannot do, because it can only measure this one. On unified memory
# a peer with a desktop session resident is not a slow launch, it is rank 1
# refusing at the memory check a minute in.
# REQUIRE_IDLE_GPU=false

# Rendezvous. Auto-detected from the default route.
# MASTER_ADDR=192.168.1.70
# PEER=poseidon

# Leave IB_HCA unset unless a log shows the wrong RDMA device chosen - measured
# here, NCCL discovers both ACTIVE ports and skips the two DOWN ones. Their
# recipe pins it; docs/decisions.md#two-node-vllm is why this repo does not.
# IB_HCA=rocep1s0f0,roceP2p1s0f0

# 8896, so it does not collide with the other serving workspaces.
# PORT=8896

# Escape hatches.
# EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS=--kv-cache-memory=41360080896
# IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai:qwen38-flash-next
